<BaseLayout title="How the AI query fanout tool works" canonicalPath="/methodology" alternatePath="/de/methode" description="How the free tool creates ten modelled follow-up searches with strict privacy, quota, cost and evidence limits."><header class="page-head"><h1>How the free tool works</h1><div class="page-head-copy"><p>A keyword goes in. Ten modelled follow-up searches come back, each with intent and a short reason.</p><p class="meta-line">Tool modelled-fanout-tool/2.0.0 · OpenRouter · owner Matthias Ramahi</p></div></header><div class="document-layout"><aside class="document-aside"><dl><div><dt>Availability</dt><dd>Live and free</dd></div><div><dt>Models</dt><dd>3 allowlisted</dd></div><div><dt>Output</dt><dd>10 queries</dd></div><div><dt>Time limit</dt><dd>20 seconds</dd></div></dl></aside><article class="document-body"><h2>One run, one selected model.</h2><p class="document-intro">The tool asks the selected model to build a compact research plan. It does not inspect ChatGPT, Google, private retrieval traces, system prompts or chain of thought.</p><ol class="controls">{steps.map(([title,copy],index)=><li><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></div></li>)}</ol><section><h2>Why this is called modelled fanout</h2><p>The ten queries are generated from a documented instruction and strict output schema. They are plausible research branches produced by the selected model. They are not proof of searches that ChatGPT, Gemini, Google or another product secretly performed.</p></section><section><h2>How to use the result</h2><p>Use it to spot different user needs, comparison angles, local questions and missing explanations. Do not treat it as search volume, ranking data or an instruction to publish ten pages. Demand and page decisions need separate evidence.</p></section><section><h2>Responsibility</h2><p>Matthias Ramahi owns method versions, corrections, reviewer status and the monthly cost envelope. No independent provider benchmark is claimed.</p></section></article></div></BaseLayout>
